  "limitations": [
    "All six fields already include the complete modeled assembly, six panels and 66 screw springs. Generic 1000 N/mm axial/lateral Hillman spring stiffness is an unqualified assumption; panel presence does not establish physical load sharing or complete screw strength.",
    "The rectangular torsion mathematics was independently checked in the prior audit. Common twist, area-proportional direct shear and intact ligament bridges at short loaded bore zones remain an engineering construction, not a verified three-dimensional joint stress bound.",
    "Separate shear and torsion peak addition remains a conservative worksheet construction. Selected compatible midface probes cannot replace an all-point bound.",
    "Reduced bolt interaction and elastic axial/bending/shear are distinct references; neither clears wood bearing, loaded edges or complete-joint behavior.",
    "Plywood rows retain both leaves, through-thickness pressure and full force/first moment. The force-only lower comparison cannot clear the balanced row comparison. The NDS-style row/APA input combination remains an engineering extension.",
    "Perfect plywood bonding, uniform 139.7 mm trapezoid beam approximation, gross timber response, first-order kinematics, stated restraints and the unverified no-slip floor hypothesis retain their original applicability limits. No actual adhesive or floor is qualified.",
    "The eight upper axes remain geometry-ineligible in all six cases. Correcting side-core breadth does not change their edges, pair spacing, bolt forces or joint eligibility."
  ],
